WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.358 --> 00:00:15.083
Welcome to Mawsynram, India!

2
00:00:15.084 --> 00:00:19.957
This village sits high in the hills below the Himalaya Mountains.

3
00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:26.096
Mawsynram is famous for something: it's the wettest place on earth!

4
00:00:26.097 --> 00:00:32.695
Every year Mawsynram gets over 11,870 millimeters of rain.

5
00:00:32.696 --> 00:00:40.058
That's enough to fill a rain gauge as tall as a four-story building!

6
00:00:40.059 --> 00:00:45.332
Ninety percent of this rain falls from April to September.

7
00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:48.784
What makes Mawsynram get so much rain?

8
00:00:48.785 --> 00:00:52.951
An annual wind system called a monsoon.

9
00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:57.515
There is a wet monsoon and a dry monsoon.

10
00:00:57.516 --> 00:01:03.792
During the wet monsoon, the wind comes from the southwest.

11
00:01:03.793 --> 00:01:06.905
It brings water from the ocean.

12
00:01:06.906 --> 00:01:10.433
Clouds form and travel with the wind.

13
00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:14.539
But the Himalaya Mountains block the clouds over Mawsynram.

14
00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:19.913
So rain falls . . . and falls and falls!

15
00:01:19.914 --> 00:01:24.868
So much rain makes Mawsynram green and beautiful.

16
00:01:24.869 --> 00:01:29.775
But living in this monster monsoon is not easy!

17
00:01:29.776 --> 00:01:34.477
There is frequent flooding and a lot of mud.

18
00:01:34.478 --> 00:01:38.337
There is too much water to raise crops.

19
00:01:38.338 --> 00:01:43.898
So people must grow and store food during the dry season.

20
00:01:43.899 --> 00:01:46.269
Or they buy food at the market.

21
00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:50.475
They must also store wood for fuel.

22
00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:55.799
Oh, and the pounding rain makes a lot of noise!

23
00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:01.625
People use grass to soundproof their tin roofs.

24
00:02:01.626 --> 00:02:06.816
Clouds often drift through houses and everything gets wet!

25
00:02:06.817 --> 00:02:11.451
Women weave grass umbrellas so that people can work in the rain.

26
00:02:11.452 --> 00:02:15.911
These umbrellas cover the body—just like a turtle's shell!

27
00:02:15.912 --> 00:02:21.389
Even with those umbrellas, getting around Mawsynram can be tough.

28
00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.452
Roads wash away.

29
00:02:24.453 --> 00:02:29.402
And wooden bridges rot within a few years.

30
00:02:29.403 --> 00:02:33.892
So people build "living" bridges.

31
00:02:33.893 --> 00:02:38.400
First they lay bamboo across streams.

32
00:02:38.401 --> 00:02:43.430
Then they tie tree roots onto the bamboo.

33
00:02:43.431 --> 00:02:49.938
The roots grow across the stream and into the soil on the other side.

34
00:02:49.939 --> 00:02:55.535
The bamboo rots away. But the roots form a living bridge.

35
00:02:55.536 --> 00:03:00.854
The oldest living bridge is over five hundred years old!

36
00:03:00.855 --> 00:03:06.905
Whew! After so many months of rain, people are ready to dry off.

37
00:03:06.906 --> 00:03:10.352
The dry monsoon starts in the autumn.

38
00:03:10.353 --> 00:03:14.995
Dry desert air blows in from the northeast.

39
00:03:14.996 --> 00:03:19.634
The rain finally stops and the water drains away.

40
00:03:19.635 --> 00:03:23.686
But the dry monsoon brings a different problem.

41
00:03:23.687 --> 00:03:31.362
Now people have too little water—in the wettest place on earth!
